<title>UK: Royal &amp; Sun interim profit beats forecasts.</title>
<headline>Royal &amp; Sun interim profit beats forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>pro forma interim for 1996</p>
<p>				   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating shr (pence)  20.3	  vs 26.4</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 6.5	   vs 5.9 Sun, 4.7 Royal</p>
<p> Pre-tax operating	450	   vs 514</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pro-forma interim pre-tax operating profits were in a range of 350 to 435 million stg.  </p>
<p> Net premiums written   4,883		  vs 4,686</p>
<p> General business	 3,730		  vs 3,661</p>
<p> Long term business     1,153		  vs 1,025</p>
<p> Pretax		     541		    vs 537</p>
<p> General business optg  358		    vs 436</p>
<p> Longterm business optg 105		    vs 98</p>
<p> Investment income	647		    vs 508</p>
<p> Interest on borrowings 35		     vs 35</p>
<p> Merger expenses	  16		     vs nil</p>
<p> Tax			  156		    vs 117</p>
<p> Net taxed		  385		    vs 420</p>
<p> Attributable	     369		    vs 412</p>
<p> Pay date		   December 2 1996</p>
<p>Div registration date  October 15 1996  Ex-div date		October 7 1996</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7721</p>
